     TO:  All
   FROM:  Kenneth Leung
   DATE:  December 28, 1989
SUBJECT:  TLXFON version C


Features:
1. Set Default Protocol to Zmodem.  (For the purpose of
   viewing File Directory.)  The original default protocol
   is Xmodem).
2. Send INIT. string when receiving an off-line (no carrier)
   signal.
3. Remain in memory as long as you like.  This way, you
   don't have to press (ALT-D) AFTER you are off-line (or
   getting busy signal, whatever.)  Simply press ENTER once
   and you are back to the phone directory.
4. Modify the status line.  Instead "Alt-Z for Help" and the
   name of the emulation (ANSI-BBS, VT100, etc.), I put the
   name of the BBS that you are currently on on there.
5. I have alternate the structure of the script for fast
   typist or a high transmitted rate modem.


Reminder:  1. If you use (ALT-K) to define a key for
              TLXFON-C.SLC, basically you can use any key
              you want.  However, it is a good idea that not
              to use (ALT-D).  It will not "POP" up the
              directory WHILE you are ON-LINE!
           2. While at DOS prompt, type the following:
                          TELIX.EXE sTLXFON-C
              will execute the TLXFON-C.SLC immediately!


ps.  In the TLXFON-C.ZIP, there is another script called
     ESC.SLC  The purpose of this script is to send ESC
     without aborting the script.  To use it, simply assign
     a key (ie. the upper-left corner key "`", any key
     except "ESC" itself) for the script.




























